mode: "100644"
text: "# Scripts, setup + two worked examples\n\n## Writing for avatar delivery\nAvatars read a script cleanly but can't ad-lib. So:\n- **One idea, conversational, short sentences.** No tongue-twisters, no rapid-fire hype.\n- **Open with the point**, not a greeting. Front-load the value.\n- Write in the brand's voice (voice-builder); add light, natural phrasing the avatar can deliver.\n- Mark **[B-ROLL]** cutaways inline so the editor knows where to break from the talking head.\n\n## The setup brief (fill before rendering)\n```\nJOB / LENGTH: explainer | training | localization | sales | faceless — target seconds\nAVATAR: stock | digital twin (consented) | talking photo (<15s)   ENGINE: Avatar IV | V\nVOICE / LANGUAGE: cloned | stock; primary + any translations (175+ via Video Translator)\nBACKGROUND / TEMPLATE / BRANDKIT: per brand-profile\nB-ROLL PLAN: where to cut away (veo-3 / screen-record / text)\nDISCLOSURE: caption + on-screen label plan\nCONSENT: confirmed for any likeness? (required)\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 — faceless explainer (blunt indie-founder voice, ~30s)\n```\nAVATAR: stock (faceless channel)   ENGINE: Avatar IV   VOICE: stock, dry/calm\nSCRIPT:\n\"Most freelancers get surprised by tax. Not because it's hard — because of one missing step.\n[B-ROLL: screen-record of a bank app, two accounts]\nMove thirty percent of every invoice into a second account the day it lands.\nThat's it. You never see the money, so you never spend it.\n[B-ROLL: calendar flipping to April, calm]\nBoring. Works. Saved me a very bad April.\"\nDISCLOSURE: on-screen \"AI presenter\" + caption note. CONSENT: n/a (stock).\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — localized founder twin (warm studio voice, ~25s, 6 languages)\n```\nAVATAR: founder Digital Twin (Avatar V, consented)   VOICE: cloned founder voice\nSCRIPT (EN master, then Video Translator → 175+ langs, lip-sync):\n\"If tax season makes your stomach drop -- this is for you.\nWe use one account and one rule, and the panic just... goes.\n[B-ROLL: tidy desk, banking app]\nMove thirty percent the day a client pays. Small step -- big calm.\"\nLOCALIZE: translate the master; keep the founder's cloned voice in each language.\nDISCLOSURE: \"Created with an AI avatar of our founder\" + EU AI Act / TikTok auto.\nCONSENT: founder consent verified for the twin.\n```\n\n## Notes\n- Keep clips short and **cut away** so the face doesn't fatigue (TALK's K).\n- A 5-minute monologue → break into segments; don't use a Talking Photo beyond ~15s.\n- Generative B-roll comes from **veo-3 / ai-video**; long→Short cutdowns from\n  **captions-and-clipping**. Finished video → scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial.\n"
